<newsitem itemid="465738" id="root" date="1997-03-25" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Foodcorp half yr shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>Foodcorp half yr shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to February 28, 1997</p>
<p>(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, attrib (cts)</p>
<p>    - before conversion   143.7	 vs    124.8</p>
<p>    - converted	     130.0	 vs    113.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 32.0	  vs    67.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   69.0	  vs    60.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   97.0	  vs    82.0</p>
<p>    Tax			 27.0	  vs    21.0</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   3.0	   vs    5.0 received</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,607.0     vs    1,526.0</p>
<p>Div payable May 16</p>
<p>on register March 27</p>
<p>Full name: Foocorp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said the group should be able to achieve its forecast of 12-15 percent growth for the full year, despite ongoing strong competition in the food industry. Steps had been taken to reduce exposure to the volatile red meat business and further cost reductions made in the commodity businesses, they said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
